# docs/roadmap.md is machine-managed by harness roadmap tooling, and its schema
# requires each `- **Key:** value` field to be ONE physical line. Prettier's
# `proseWrap: "always"` wraps them, and harness then reads only the first line
# and silently discards the rest — no error on either side. A shard + regen
# round-trip took the file from 40,525 bytes to 11,640 before this entry existed.
#
# This is not a style preference and it is not dead config. `.harness/hooks/
# quality-warner.js` runs `prettier --check` on every file written in this repo
# and blocks on violation, so without this line an agent cannot write a correct
# roadmap at all — the hook forces the broken shape.
#
# Removing this entry silently re-breaks the file. The guard that FAILS when it
# happens is ts/test/roadmap-field-contract.test.ts; keep the two in sync — if
# sharded output is ever committed, extend the ignore and that test's file list
# together, in one change. See docs/changes/roadmap-priority-and-field-contract/
# and AGENTS.md.
docs/roadmap.md
